---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Why a whole page for 50 KB?',
    a: 'Because 50 KB is the size the strict doors ask for: application forms, listing photos, profile and document uploads that reject anything bigger. This page is the Compress image bench with the target already set to 50 KB, so the job is two clicks: pick the photo, run.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How exact is the result?',
    a: 'On a normal photo, our bench landed within about half a percent of the target. The page searches quality and, when quality alone has no setting close enough (which happens on very noisy photos), the dimensions too, and it shows you the exact final size and how far it sits from 50 KB.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a 50 KB photo look like?',
    a: 'Softer than the original, and sometimes smaller in dimensions too; there is no free way to keep every pixel at this size. The result line always states the quality and dimensions used, and the preview shows the photo itself, so you can judge the trade before you download.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my photo go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is decoded, re-encoded and offered back to you inside this page. Nothing is uploaded.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
---

<Base title="Compress an image to 50 KB, free, in your browser · Benchzy" description="Shrink a photo under a 50 KB limit for forms and listings, with the work done inside your browser. No upload, no account. The achieved size and its distance from the target are shown.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Job ticket · image bench · preset 50 KB</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Compress image to 50 KB</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        The form said: photo, under 50 KB. This page is set to that target before you start. Pick
        the photo, run the job, and take away a JPEG that fits, with the exact size it landed at
        printed on the result. Everything runs in your browser; the photo is never uploaded.
        A different target lives on the <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/compress-image/">Compress image page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="ci-tool" data-preset-kb="50" data-lock-target="1">
      <div id="ci-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick an image">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a photo on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">JPG, PNG or WebP · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="ci-file" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,.jpg,.jpeg,.png,.webp" class="hidden" />
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Target size</h2>
          <p class="font-display text-3xl font-black mt-3">50 KB</p>
          <p class="text-ink-soft text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3 max-w-md">
            Fixed by this page, the form and seller preset. The bench searches quality first, then
            dimensions when quality alone cannot land close.
          </p>
          <img id="ci-preview" alt="The compressed result" class="hidden w-full border border-line bg-paper-deep object-contain max-h-72 mt-6" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="ci-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <button id="ci-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Compress to 50 KB</button>
          <p id="ci-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a photo to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="ci-result" class="hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="ci-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="ci-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="ci-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the photo (JPG)</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page decodes your photo and runs a search: it encodes at different quality settings,
          watches the sizes, and closes in on 50 KB. On hard photos, quality alone has no setting
          that lands close (the steps jump over the window), so the search then adjusts the
          dimensions too. That combined search is the shipping method here; on the hardest photo on
          our bench it landed within about a third of a percent of the target.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          At 50 KB a big photo gives up a lot: expect a softer picture, and on noisy photos a
          smaller one. The result line always states the quality and dimensions used. If a photo is
          already under 50 KB and already a JPEG, you get it back unchanged. The output is a JPEG,
          which suits the forms and listings this preset is built for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/compress-image.js';
  </script>
</Base>
